{
	quest.02B5E57E9E803F78.quest_desc: [
		"We bind an iron plate on a Binding array along with a charged gem, and the metal wakes up. &cSentient Armour&r starts small — a hundred points of room to grow — but it keeps a long memory."
		""
		"It logs everything we do: hits taken, distance walked, blocks broken. Slowly the piece stops being generic and starts being ours."
	]
	quest.02B5E57E9E803F78.title: "The Sentient Shell"
	quest.09DEA44456CD5010.quest_desc: [
		"We perform the &cBreaching the Edge of Demon Realm&r rite and tear a one-time wound through the veil in a single move — on the other side, an &cAntechamber&r opens up."
		""
		"We step through. Best to carry keys, or at least a way to find them, because the deeper realm won't open its doors for free."
	]
	quest.09DEA44456CD5010.title: "Breaching the Veil"
	quest.0BA0AA8A6F07D383.quest_desc: [
		"We brew an &cArcane Scribe Tool&r in the &cTabula Vitae&r, our first alchemical bench. With an Orb of Vitae seated in it, the bench pulls EV straight from our Anima to prepare this tool, along with reagents and our earliest anointments."
		""
		"We strike the ground with it and a circle wakes under our feet — our first &6Alchemy Array&r."
	]
	quest.0BA0AA8A6F07D383.title: "The Scribe's Tool"
	quest.11F6669733F1420B.quest_desc: [
		"We reach 52 runes in total: the 24 we already had, plus a third ring, deeper still, with pillars crowned in blood-stained glass. We seal the four corners with &cPolished Bloodstone&r, cut from Tau Fruit."
		""
		"This is where we forge the &cMagus Orb of Vitae&r — &e1,000,000 EV&r of Anima — and the &cRitual Diviner [Dusk]&r, which opens up a much wider repertoire of rites."
	]
	quest.11F6669733F1420B.title: "Tier III: The Master's Orb"
	quest.19891A8F26FBAB0A.quest_desc: [
		"Every reagent we brew in the Tabula Vitae hides a sigil waiting to be scribed: water that never runs out, lava on tap, a void that swallows liquid, haste, magnetism, faster growth."
		""
		"Crafting just one shows us the whole family — a Vitaemancer with a full sigil belt is never caught without an option."
	]
	quest.19891A8F26FBAB0A.quest_subtitle: "Any one proves the point."
	quest.19891A8F26FBAB0A.title: "A Belt Full of Sigils"
	quest.1B6642BBDAEB2BD5.quest_desc: ["We can only forge the &cVeneficus Orb of Vitae&r once the altar sits at Tier II, and it's worth the wait: it swaps the Discipulus's tight reserve for &e150,000 EV&r of breathing room — six times what we had."]
	quest.1B6642BBDAEB2BD5.title: "Tier II: The Magician's Orb"
	quest.1BBABB2106D321A4.quest_desc: [
		"A &cSpike Trap&r feeds the altar every time it hurts a creature within 8 blocks of an Ara Vitae. We craft one and keep creatures coming — a spawner or a Vortex Array both do the job."
		""
		"With a collection array nearby to grab the drops, the altar starts feeding itself while we go handle something else."
	]
	quest.1BBABB2106D321A4.title: "Early Blood Automation"
	quest.1F7ACF813D8804A6.quest_desc: [
		"The &cAlchemy Array&r wants two offerings at once. Some pairings craft entirely new objects from scratch — that's how our very first sigil, the &cDivination Sigil&r, comes to be — others just fire an effect right there, out into the world around us."
		""
		"Worth trying a combination just to watch the circle answer."
	]
	quest.1F7ACF813D8804A6.title: "Circle of Intent"
	quest.22CB17C102BB6773.quest_desc: [
		"&cTau Oil&r takes the Athanor's Cutting Fluid from Basic to Intermediate, and it's the base for the stronger anointments that keep our blades and bows deadly for much longer."
		""
		"It also gives rise to Spiritus Catalysts, which speed up crystal growth — or change what a crystal grows into entirely."
	]
	quest.22CB17C102BB6773.title: "Refining the Tau"
	quest.24C0619EB4A13CA3.quest_desc: [
		"At the core of everything we build sits a network of routing nodes — the piping that carries items, fluids, and even energy, all through the same lines."
		""
		"We place a &cMaster Routing Node&r first; every other node auto-connects to the nearest master the moment we set it down nearby."
	]
	quest.24C0619EB4A13CA3.title: "Laying the Veins"
	quest.298458E916F65407.quest_desc: ["We burn Spiritus in the &cVas Maleficum&r and the chunk's air thickens with will. Whatever we release into it, we can read back later — a hidden reservoir capped at &e100 per Aspect&r."]
	quest.298458E916F65407.title: "The Aura Between Worlds"
	quest.2E22A601DC126B7B.quest_desc: [
		"A crystal doesn't grow on its own, it comes out of a saturated Spiritus Aura. Where the aura sits thickest, the &cCrystallarium Maleficum&r seeds a cluster that slowly pulls in Spiritus of its own type."
		""
		"Once the cluster forms, we can move it off the Crystallarium to let it grow further — but the aura needs to sit fully saturated at &e100&r of that type, or the crystal simply won't grow."
	]
	quest.2E22A601DC126B7B.quest_subtitle: "The crystalline cradle."
	quest.2E22A601DC126B7B.title: "Crystals from Nothing"
	quest.383F7F715C60252B.quest_desc: [
		"We add sixteen more runes in a second ring, one level deeper and wider than the first, and raise four pillars at the cardinal sides, each capped in &bBlood Stained Glass&r. Twenty-four runes, all told."
		""
		"From here the altar stops being just a tool and starts turning into an engine — Rituals and Sentient Armor both sit right past this point."
	]
	quest.383F7F715C60252B.title: "Tier II: The Second Ring"
	quest.3CA324BE8531F253.quest_desc: [
		"Fully saturated Tau, worked through the Athanor, finally condenses into a &cWeak Blood Shard&r — the piece that finishes the Tier III pillars and opens the door to everything past them."
		""
		"It's also the base for stronger anointments and the potion catalysts that keep our gear deadly for much longer."
	]
	quest.3CA324BE8531F253.title: "The Weak Blood Shard"
	quest.3F2FE793CE5052F0.quest_desc: ["Nodes auto-connect to the nearest master when placed, but if we want to hand-reassign one to a different Master Routing Node, the &cNode Router&r tool handles it in a single click."]
	quest.3F2FE793CE5052F0.title: "Rerouting the Network"
	quest.40C32A4F6DE4B782.quest_desc: [
		"Tau on its own is only potential. It's the &cAthanor&r that does the heavy work — pressing &cTau Oil&r from the fruit and saturating the rest into the shards a higher altar will demand from us."
		""
		"Worth building this furnace carefully; almost every material chain from here on runs through it."
	]
	quest.40C32A4F6DE4B782.title: "The Athanor"
	quest.419DB4A2A5A5FC58.quest_desc: [
		"Someone runs these mines, and doesn't clock out easily. The &cForeman&r is a Daemonium Doloris swollen with authority — six hundred hearts of spite guarding a key nobody else carries."
		""
		"We're taking the &cMine Entrance Key&r off him. It won't be without a fight."
	]
	quest.419DB4A2A5A5FC58.title: "The Foreman"
	quest.4393ADF3E4C8B0D4.quest_desc: [
		"Raw will bends toward a purpose. With a catalyst and an Animus Mote pulled from a Daemonium Animaris, we turn a &cRaw&r cluster into &cRuina&r, &cNihilum&r, &cVindicta&r, or &cInvictus&r."
		""
		"Each aspect changes how our Sentient Tools behave, and each one refines rituals differently through the Ritual Configurator."
	]
	quest.4393ADF3E4C8B0D4.quest_subtitle: "Any one aspect proves the craft."
	quest.4393ADF3E4C8B0D4.title: "The Five Aspects"
	quest.46122A9389875512.quest_desc: [
		"This is where Vitaemancy shows us its real size. Every ritual needs a heart: we set a &cMaster Ritual Stone&r in the middle, mark the lesser stones around it with the &cRitual Diviner&r, and wake the working with a &cWeak Activation Crystal&r."
		""
		"Over thirty catalogued rituals are waiting for us, from the Well of Suffering to the Endless Quarry — each one does work for us that would otherwise cost our own blood."
	]
	quest.46122A9389875512.title: "Rites and Rituals"
	quest.4694863405CFB97B.quest_desc: [
		"Past a Spatial Distortion sits the entrance to the &cMines&r. &cMine Dungeon Keys&r open the way in, toward the veins of Demonite."
		""
		"What haunts these halls isn't a bunch of reskinned villagers — it's ten different kinds of Daemonium, each fighting its own way. We learn them by fighting them."
	]
	quest.4694863405CFB97B.title: "The Mines"
	quest.4840F41B536529E3.quest_desc: ["A flask is an effect we hold in our hand. A &cTipped Throwing Dagger&r is that same effect delivered straight to someone else's throat, no need to get close at all."]
	quest.4840F41B536529E3.title: "A Sharper Point"
	quest.4AE0C2D2D8D145F6.quest_desc: ["The standard key opens the Endless Realm's common doors, but there's a &cMine Key&r cut specifically for the entrance guarded deep within — the one the Foreman doesn't let go of easily."]
	quest.4AE0C2D2D8D145F6.title: "Deeper Locks"
	quest.4EBC5B191A7B12D9.quest_desc: [
		"Runes are what push the altar up a tier. To climb, we lay them in rings around the basin, each new ring a bit deeper and wider than the last, with pillars or capstones joining in at higher tiers."
		""
		"Every rune starts out &cblank&r — no purpose at all — until we carve one into it: capacity, speed, or sacrifice."
	]
	quest.4EBC5B191A7B12D9.title: "Blank Runes"
	quest.4EE580588CC10C4E.quest_desc: ["We dig out the veins the Foreman used to guard. &cDemonite&r is the only real source of Hellforged metal, the material that carries the altar's final tiers."]
	quest.4EE580588CC10C4E.title: "Demonite"
	quest.4F77EDCEB49EB67F.quest_desc: ["With luck, we pull Intricate &cHellforged Parts&r from deep in the dungeon. Paired with Netherite Scrap, upgrading any rune with one doubles the value it already gave our altar."]
	quest.4F77EDCEB49EB67F.title: "Doubling Down on Runes"
	quest.538E28637FF76912.quest_desc: ["This Quest has been authored by &6AllTheMods Staff&r, or a &2Community contributor&r for use in AllTheMods Modpacks. \\n\\nAs all &6AllTheMods&r packs are licensed under &eAll Rights Reserved&r, this Quest is not allowed to be used in any public packs not released by &6AllTheMods Team&r without explicit permission. \\n\\nThis quest is intentionally hidden, if you're seeing this, you're in editing mode."]
	quest.54AB11938676D4C7.quest_desc: [
		"Blood doesn't just multiply power, it multiplies wealth too. We brew &cCutting Fluid&r in the Tabula Vitae and dissolve an ore in it: the slab strips the metal from the stone, two dust for every ore we offer."
		""
		"We smelt that dust into a finished ingot — double what a normal furnace pulls from the same rock."
	]
	quest.54AB11938676D4C7.title: "Alchemy of Ore"
	quest.564AD8763F753C74.quest_desc: [
		"If raising the altar starts to feel slow, there's another road open: &6potioncrafting&r unlocks as soon as we hit Tier I. We can brew &cAlchemy Flasks&r carrying dozens of effects to drink or throw whenever we need them."
		""
		"Nobody walking around with a full flask belt is ever really unprotected."
	]
	quest.564AD8763F753C74.title: "Bottled Effects"
	quest.56DDCB2865CEB9D3.quest_desc: ["The &cSpiritus Aura Gauge&r shows the local concentration of will nearby. Sneaking while holding it gives us exact numbers per Aspect, from &e0 to 100&r — handy when we're deciding where to grow our next crystal."]
	quest.56DDCB2865CEB9D3.title: "Reading the Aura"
	quest.56F4E4845B8F12BB.quest_desc: [
		"Not every offering to the altar needs to become an orb — this one becomes a foundation. Smooth stone, run through a &cTier 0&r Ara Vitae for &e1,000 EV&r, turns into &cTabula Rasa&r: deepslate ready for the first marks we carve into it."
		""
		"It's what we'll scribe almost every sigil onto, and it's only the first rung of a longer ladder — Robur, Animata, Spiritus, and finally Aetherea, each one asking for a stronger altar and more blood."
	]
	quest.56F4E4845B8F12BB.title: "The Blank Slate"
	quest.5785D68A5F1ED2D2.quest_desc: [
		"Only the Antechamber, past the veil, grows this strange fruit. &cWeak Tau&r carries a piece of the demon realm's own vitality — we carry it home and let animals walk over it."
		""
		"They take a little damage over time, and every tick there's a chance the fruit saturates further, until it ripens at last into &cStrong Tau&r, dense enough to refine."
	]
	quest.5785D68A5F1ED2D2.title: "The Tau Harvest"
	quest.58248AF507380501.quest_desc: [
		"An enchantment is a woven thing, and what's woven can be undone. We load the Athanor with a stack of plain books and a single enchanted item — armour, a tool, even an enchanted book works."
		""
		"The crucible lifts one enchantment at a time onto a fresh book, cleaning the original off. We salvage what would've been wasted, or take apart something rare to reforge it our own way."
	]
	quest.58248AF507380501.title: "Enchantment Salvaging"
	quest.5AA17C1657E8E5DE.quest_desc: [
		"We carve upgrades onto our Sentient Armour with &cUpgrade Tomes&r. One click adds a level; sneak and use to bank the maximum at once."
		""
		"Body Builder, Repair, Fierce Strike, Dwarven Might — we build the body that fits how we play."
	]
	quest.5AA17C1657E8E5DE.title: "Wear It In"
	quest.5ACB4565C6B2466C.quest_desc: [
		"A &cCrystal Catalyst&r speeds up the growth of a similarly aspected cluster: a raw catalyst on a raw crystal makes it grow noticeably faster."
		""
		"An &caspected&r catalyst goes further still — it flips the growing crystal's type over to the new aspect entirely."
	]
	quest.5ACB4565C6B2466C.title: "Coaxing Crystals"
	quest.5C3EA8B4F5949406.quest_desc: [
		"The &cHellfire Forge&r eats &6Spiritus&r, the residue we tear from creatures wounded by our daggers or our blade. Feed it Spiritus Gems and it pays us back in kind: more gems, &cSentient Tools&r, volatile charges, and more."
		""
		"It never stops being hungry. We keep it fed."
	]
	quest.5C3EA8B4F5949406.title: "The Hellfire Forge"
	quest.602884068EC40EDB.quest_desc: [
		"A &cSentient Sword&r harvests far more Spiritus than any thrown dagger, and it gets stronger the more will we feed it over time — a weapon that carries the memory of every fight."
		""
		"Expensive this early on, but it pays off."
	]
	quest.602884068EC40EDB.title: "Sentient Steel"
	quest.6101AB772B0317F1.quest_desc: [
		"We can't manage what we can't measure. The &cDivination Sigil&r, scribed on the Alchemy Array, shows how much Anima we're holding and how much EV an altar in front of us has stored."
		""
		"Craft the &cSeer's Sigil&r too and we get even more: exact progress, EV per tick, charge reserve. We'll need that once we start aiming for higher tiers."
	]
	quest.6101AB772B0317F1.title: "A Sense for Anima"
	quest.65BD73DA55BCC624.quest_desc: [
		"&cBlood is the currency of power here.&r We start with nothing but a knife and a wound, and from those first drops we will raise an altar that can drink whole ecosystems dry, tie our soul to a hundred reservoirs, turn demons into tools, and tear open a dimension that wants us dead."
		""
		"We call this craft &6Vitaemancy&r — turning blood into &cEssentia Vitae&r (EV), the fuel behind every altar, sigil, ritual and forge we're about to build."
		""
		"Our first step is simple: set an &cAra Vitae&r on flat stone we can walk all the way around. It has no blood of its own yet, so it borrows a little from whoever stands nearby — never enough to kill, just enough to wake it up."
	]
	quest.65BD73DA55BCC624.quest_subtitle: "A journey written in blood."
	quest.65BD73DA55BCC624.title: "Welcome to Neo Vitae"
	quest.671F7551CBDF462F.quest_desc: [
		"The &cHighway to Hell&r ritual opens a permanent gate into the Endless Realm. We go in armed and armored; nobody unprepared comes out of this well."
		""
		"The deeper we push, the more signs we'll see of rifts opening or something stirring below. New door types — like the mine entrance — unlock as we go; worth watching for them and picking the right key at the right time."
	]
	quest.671F7551CBDF462F.title: "Highway to Hell"
	quest.702FC3E5D0D6C31F.quest_desc: [
		"We close the widest ring of all and reach 172 runes in total. Tall pillars rise at the cardinal sides, crowned with &cCrystal Clusters&r — this is the Ara Vitae in its final form, unmatched in capacity and crafting power."
		""
		"The &cDivinus Orb of Vitae&r caps it off: &e10,000,000 EV&r of Anima. We asked what this power costs. Now we know: everything, handed over a drop at a time, until asking and answering become the same act."
	]
	quest.702FC3E5D0D6C31F.quest_subtitle: "What you do with that power is yours to decide."
	quest.702FC3E5D0D6C31F.title: "Tier V: The Pinnacle"
	quest.70D2718D54785867.quest_desc: [
		"We run an ore block through the whole Athanor chain to ingots, then use &cCorrupted Dust&r with ore fragments in the Tabula Vitae to double them into &cOre Gravel&r."
		""
		"With the Spiritus cycle maxed out, we can push a raw ore past &e8x&r the yield of a normal smelt."
	]
	quest.70D2718D54785867.title: "The Crucible's Greed"
	quest.71E0D06EA65172CF.quest_desc: [
		"We don't need to watch everything bleed out slowly. A plain &cThrowing Dagger&r covers us at range early on, and it kicks off something bigger: our whole &6Spiritus&r economy."
		""
		"Whatever we wound with a thrown dagger leaves &cRaw Spiritus&r behind when it dies. Pick it up — the Hellfire Forge is going to want it."
	]
	quest.71E0D06EA65172CF.title: "Throwing Daggers"
	quest.73391A08D7615C77.quest_desc: [
		"We lay a &bdiamond&r on the still-empty altar. Two thousand EV, pulled from whoever is nearby, is enough to turn it into our first &cNovicius Orb of Vitae&r — the anchor for our &6Anima&r, the hidden network that will carry our soul into everything we craft from here on."
		""
		"One right-click binds the orb to us for good. After that we can offer our own blood whenever we want: near an altar it pours straight into the basin, and away from one it simply waits inside the orb until we're ready."
		""
		"Even this first, humble orb pushes our Anima up to &e5,000 EV&r. It's the smallest of six steps, but every step after this one depends on it."
	]
	quest.73391A08D7615C77.title: "Bind a Novicius Orb"
	quest.759B0D6F8C0CC1EF.quest_desc: [
		"Eight &cBlank Runes&r already close our first ring, one level below the basin, in a 3x3 shape with the center left open. The four cardinal slots take specialized runes; we leave the diagonals alone for now — they only matter at higher tiers."
		""
		"With the altar at this tier, we can also carry a bound orb in our off-hand and pull EV straight from whatever we kill, sparing our own blood."
	]
	quest.759B0D6F8C0CC1EF.quest_subtitle: "Altar upgrade."
	quest.759B0D6F8C0CC1EF.title: "Tier I: The Ring of Runes"
	quest.7731623EA92027D9.quest_desc: [
		"We reach 100 runes in total, with one more ring, deeper still, stacked on top of the previous ones. A &cHellforged Block&r closes each of the four cardinal points, and the altar climbs to &cTier IV&r — home to the most destructive rites in all of Vitaemancy."
		""
		"Here we forge the &cDominus Orb of Vitae&r — &e5,000,000 EV&r of Anima, a thousand times what our very first orb gave us."
	]
	quest.7731623EA92027D9.title: "Tier IV: The Archmage's Orb"
	quest.7AFEB7A91DC8F413.quest_desc: [
		"The Novicius Orb no longer holds enough for us. Once the altar reaches Tier I, we can forge the &cDiscipulus Orb of Vitae&r instead — it stores far more and drains faster too."
		""
		"With it, our Anima's ceiling climbs to &e25,000 EV&r — five times what we had before."
	]
	quest.7AFEB7A91DC8F413.title: "The Apprentice's Orb"
	quest.7B293C32824033F9.quest_desc: [
		"The &cCrystallum Fractura&r ritual automates the harvest for us: it doubles the growth speed of every crystal type in range and picks each one the moment it matures."
		""
		"For every fully-grown crystal it collects, it applies bonus Fortune scaled to the chunk's Raw Spiritus. We activate it, and let it run on its own."
	]
	quest.7B293C32824033F9.title: "Activate the Crystallum Fractura"
	quest.7C7C061FC04B89FB.quest_desc: ["Demonite, once refined, becomes &cHellforged Ingots&r — the backbone of nearly everything we'll build in the endgame."]
	quest.7C7C061FC04B89FB.title: "Hellforged Steel"
	quest.7CF9A68167ADAD1A.quest_desc: [
		"We forge a &cMaster Routing Node Core&r to raise how much the network carries per transmission, and a &cSpeed Core&r to send those transmissions more often."
		""
		"We seat as many as we want. A network fed like that can move oceans in moments."
	]
	quest.7CF9A68167ADAD1A.title: "A Sluggish Heart Serves No One"
	task.6D5BE02E9FAED45C.title: "AllRightsReserved"
	task.7DA13EB040BC1C19.title: "AllRightsReserved"
}
